  "conclusion": "Two independent current-boot KFD-instrumented 128K warmup-plus-three processes complete exactly at merged commit babbc8c6, so this campaign establishes idle, healthy-active, and post-termination KFD baselines but does not capture the intermittent stall. During both healthy-active snapshots the GPU is doing real work at 97-99% reported activity and 128-129 W, yet /sys/kernel/debug/kfd/rls says 'No active runlist'. Therefore rls alone is not a usable active-versus-stalled discriminator on this MES-managed gfx1151 configuration. KFD mqds and sysfs do expose the process and the same three queue objects in both runs: two compute queues (4 KiB and 1 MiB rings) and one SDMA queue (8 MiB ring), with zero fault/page-in/page-out counters and only 3-4 ms cumulative eviction time. No HQD dump is taken because the predeclared protocol reserves that large, potentially perturbing read for an established stall. The two completions do not prove lifecycle stability or a merged-code fix after the prior repeated failures; timing-sensitive debugfs reads and the chunk recorder can perturb incidence. Proceed to the prepared MES-log diagnostic boot, retaining these snapshots as the healthy control and capturing HQDs only if no-progress reproduces.",
